title: lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/tw5/tiddlers/sigil-kukali
tags: $:/tags/Global lar:///ha.ka.ba/tags/SharktoothSigil
lar-kind: leaf
lar-pono-uri: lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kukali
lar-see-also: \suspends
lar-pattern: <<~\s*kukali(?:\s+trigger[=:]"?([\w.-]+)"?)?\s*>>
lar-example: <<~ kukali trigger="on-score">>
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

<!-- kukali — a WAIT inside a causal island, until a named trigger fires:

         <<~ kukali trigger="on-score">>

     //kūkali// waits, patient, remaining in suspense. The island parks rather than freezes, and it
     resumes EXACTLY ONCE — subscribeOnce semantics. `trigger` names the `#slot` fragment of a
     papalohe wire in the same carrier; omitted, the wait takes the first reaction that arrives.
     papalohe declares the wire and kukali declares the wait at the receiving end.

     THE TRIGGER RIDES AS A NAMED PARAMETER, under either separator — `trigger="x"` and `trigger:x`
     both reach the slot, since a call binds a name through `=` and `:` alike.

     THE PAGE STAYS CLEAR. A wait governs execution and never layout, so the definition hands the
     compile layer a data annotation carrying the trigger and renders nothing. -->

\procedure ~kukali(trigger:"")
<span class="lar-kukali" data-kukali-trigger=<<trigger>> hidden="true"/>
\end
